[WorkerA] claimed T-0003: Annotate scripture verse HTML with entity spans so verse text shows person/place/thing chips in the discovery panel
[WorkerA] running claude --model sonnet …
Done. T-0003 complete:

**What was done:**
- Created `lds_pipeline/annotate_entity_spans.py` — a build-time pipeline script that pre-annotates chapter HTML files with entity data attributes
- Ran it against all 1,534 non-notes chapters
- **Results:** 1,410 chapters changed, 16,673 entity spans added across 40,493 verses

**How it works:**
1. **Step 1:** For each `span.w` in a verse, exact-matches the text content (lowercased) against scripture person/place/thing variants → adds `data-entity`, `data-place`, or `data-thing` attribute directly on the existing span
2. **Step 2:** Walks plain text nodes not inside any `.w` or `.ent-link` span, finds multi-word entity name matches (greedy longest-first, word boundaries), and wraps them in `<span class="ent-link">`

This mirrors the runtime `annotateChapterEntities()` JS function exactly, so the discovery panel chips will now populate from pre-annotated HTML. The JS will skip already-annotated spans (it checks `if (span.dataset.entity || ...) return;`).
